    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Texas?",
      "a": "Texas receives $93.5B in federal contract obligations year to date. Texas obligations come from 184,730 awards with an average award size of $506K and the total is up 8.2% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Texas?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense awards the most contracts in Texas, obligating $42.7B. The Department of Homeland Security is second with $26.7B and the Department of Veterans Affairs is third with $17.9B. Other buyers include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $1.8B and the Department of Energy with $1.7B."
